      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T12:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is all this business with the `duplicated` bool and the logic around it just to get a message that start with the package name? Isn\u0027t it overall simpler to just mention the package in the free text message instead? E.g:\n\nmodule \"\u003csome weird internal name\u003e\": Duplicate package modules in \"//top\"\n\nI think it\u0027d be good to avoid this property because it can cause uncertainty about whether duplicate packages actually are supported somehow.",
